 "text": "Hello, how are things going? A sketch is quick and rough, usually only one character, while a study is detailed and can feature multiple versions of the same subject. Kind of, yes. It' the version of character you keep refining until you' happy with it. That's a study, and a great way to improve your drawing skills. A quick sketch to capture them as they change day to day, and a study of one spot that changes over weeks months. Which one speaks to you as an easy way to spend a day or an hour? Whichever you choose, practice helps so much more than worrying about which one is real. cloud sketch is perfect, and gives you fresh material every time.",
